## Third-party code

### Odysseus — https://github.com/odysseus-dev/odysseus
Copyright (c) the Odysseus contributors. Licensed under AGPL-3.0.

Portions of the Compare, Deep Research, and Documents features are derived from
Odysseus. This project is AGPL-3.0 specifically so that such reuse is permitted.

Audited 2026-07-31. Files where Odysseus source WAS read, each carrying its own
clause 1 header and §5(a) modification notice:

  server/compare.mjs               ← routes/compare/compare_routes.py
  server/research.mjs              ← src/deep_research.py, routes/research/research_routes.py
  server/docs.mjs                  ← routes/document_routes.py
  src/sections/DocsSection.jsx     ← static/js/document.js
  src/sections/docs/AiEditBar.jsx  ← static/js/document.js

Files where Odysseus source was NOT read. These were written from its bundled demo
recordings and from capability descriptions, so clause 1 does not attach to them;
they carry the `lib/chat-protocol.mjs` wording instead. All are AGPL-3.0 anyway,
because the whole program is.

  src/ui/chatBlocks.jsx
  src/sections/CompareSection.jsx
  src/styles/compare.css
  src/sections/ResearchSection.jsx
  src/styles/research.css
  src/styles/docs.css

**Basis for the last three, stated plainly because it is weaker than the rest of
this audit.** The first three say so in their own headers. The last three did not
when this audit was written, and were briefly recorded here as unplaceable. They
are placed on the statements of the agents that wrote them, given at completion:

  · The author of `server/research.mjs`, `ResearchSection.jsx` and `research.css`
    reported consulting Odysseus source for the server module ONLY — naming
    `src/deep_research.py` and `routes/research/research_routes.py` — and stated
    that the JSX and CSS were written without reading `static/js/research/` or the
    demo recording.
  · The author of `server/docs.mjs`, `DocsSection.jsx` and `docs.css` enumerated
    exactly two consultations, `routes/document_routes.py` and
    `static/js/document.js`. `docs.css` was not among them.

That is testimony, not inspection: nobody diffed these files against Odysseus to
confirm it. It is corroborated only by `server/research.mjs` citing the two Python
files and not `static/js/research/`, which is consistent but proves nothing. The
distinction does not affect distribution — AGPL-3.0 applies either way — but it
would matter to anyone relicensing, so the strength of the evidence is recorded
here rather than smoothed over.

On that basis all three now carry the standard header wording in the files
themselves, so this paragraph records why they say it rather than being the only
place it is said.

**Obligations that come with that — these are not optional:**

1. Any file containing Odysseus-derived code carries a header naming Odysseus as
   the source and stating the file is AGPL-3.0. Add it in the same commit as the
   code, not later.
2. State what was changed. AGPL §5(a): modified files must carry prominent notice
